## 6. Step 3: Create Dockerfile

**File: Dockerfile**

```
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/*.jar app.jar

EXPOSE 8080

ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
```

**Explanation:**

| Instruction | Purpose                                       |
| ----------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| FROM        | Uses Java 17 runtime image.                   |
| WORKDIR     | Sets the working directory.                   |
| COPY        | Copies the generated JAR file into the image. |
| EXPOSE      | Documents application port 8080.              |
| ENTRYPOINT  | Starts the Java application.                  |

**Important:** The Dockerfile uses the JAR generated by Maven during the CI pipeline.

